1://! elevation — per-task root-password elevation for protected operations.
2://!
3://! Some operations change what every user gets: the Control Plane model and
4://! the router's provider profiles, and the system-wide UI catalog. Each of
5://! these is a *protected task*. Besides the caller's verified identity (the
6://! stored SID1 session) and exact grant, a protected task needs a one-time
7://! elevation ticket for that exact call: the caller enters the root
8://! password through `authorize_task`, which binds the ticket to the
9://! target plugin, method and canonical arguments. The ticket is consumed by
10://! the call it names and expires shortly after; nothing stays unlocked.
11://!
12://! Protected tasks carry polkit-style action ids so a polkit-backed authority
13://! can later replace the password check without touching the protected
14://! methods; `deploy/polkit/org.opdbus.v1.policy` declares the same ids for
15://! local D-Bus callers. This plugin is the schema of record and owns the
16://! protected-task policy; MutationEngine enforces it at its single dispatch
17://! choke point (op-grpc-bridge `task_elevation`).
18:
19:use anyhow::{Result, ensure};
20:use async_trait::async_trait;
21:use op_state::{ApplyResult, Checkpoint, DiffMetadata, PluginCapabilities, StateDiff, StatePlugin};
